The learned Single Judge who heard the appeals divided the lands into two belts and awarded compensation for the first belt up to the depth of 500 meters from the road at Rs. 15 per square yard i.e. 72,600/- per acre and fixed a flat rate of Rs. 25,000/- per acre for the remaining area. In addition, ht awarded solatium at 15% and interest at 6% per annum. While passing that order the learned judge gave the following direction;
All this, however, is subject to the claims made by them in their memorandum of appeals and cross-objections and the court fee paid thereon. Some of the claimants filed Letters Patent Appeals against the Award made by the learned Single Judge. These appeals were partly allowed in that the compensation awarded at the flat rate of Rs. 25,000/- was raised to Rs. 8 per square yard i.e. Rs. 38,720/- per acre. While making that order it was observed as under:
However, the enhancement would not exceed the amount claimed in these appeals on which court fee has already been paid.
